   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Going to the doctor in Spain",
     "texto": [
      "In Spain, to see a doctor you first call your **centro de salud** and **pides cita**. The family doctor sees you in the **consulta**; if needed, they send you to a **especialista**.\n\nThe doctor may ask for an **análisis de sangre** (sometimes you must go **en ayunas**, without eating) or give you a **receta** for the pharmacy.\n\nIf you cannot work because you are ill, the doctor gives you the **baja**: **estás de baja**. When you recover, they **dan el alta**.\n\nIf it is serious, you go to **urgencias**, and sometimes you are **ingresado** in hospital. In other countries the system is different."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Speaking politely",
     "texto": [
      "At reception and with the doctor you use **usted**:\n\n- **Quería** pedir cita. (the imperfect softens the wish and is more polite than «quiero»)\n- **Vaya** a urgencias. · **Póngase** en contacto con nosotros. (command with «usted»)\n- La doctora **le dirá** si hace falta. (the future announces what will happen)\n\nWith «usted», the pronoun is **le**, **lo** or **la**, not «te»."
     ],
